or industrial purposes to more than 80 square feet, except in accordance with this Ordinance; (h) Signs attached to the roof of a building or structure; (i) Portable signs;

- (j) Any sign that is taller than 19 feet in sign height, except in accordance with this Ordinance;

- (k) Wall signs projecting more than 24 inches from the building surface on which it is attached, except blade signs may project up to 48 inches from the building surface on which it is attached; (1) Electronic signs used as canopy, wall, or awning signs;

- (m) More than four freestanding signs on any platted, recorded, or deeded lot of record;

- (n) Signs posted without the permission of the owner of the property or their authorized tenant or agent;

- (0) Permanent or temporary window signs which cover more than 50 percent of the window glass surface of each pane of glass.

- (p) Signs which are erected or maintained upon trees, utility poles, or painted or drawn upon rocks or other natural features;

